        "Collect and convert a pressure reading using float(input(...)). Use the exact value \"Enter pressure: \".",
            /* CAVECODE_PYTHON_MODULE_6_TRANSFERPROMPT_REPAIR */
        /* CAVECODE_PYTHON_MODULE_6_TRANSFERPROMPT_REPAIR */
        "Collect and convert an integer cycle count. Use these exact identifiers: cycle_count, input, int. Use the exact value \"Enter cycle count: \".",
            "cycle_count = int(input(\"Enter cycle count: \"))",
            "The terminal can now perform math with operator-entered readings."
        ),
        new Lesson(
            "Chapter 1 · Control-Room Foundations",
            "Arithmetic",
            "Calculate an Average",
            "Arithmetic operators let Python combine sensor readings. Parentheses make the intended order easy to see.",
            "average_flow = (inlet_flow + outlet_flow) / 2",
            "average_temperature = (zone_a + zone_b) / 2",
            "average_temperature = (zone_a + zone_b) ___ 2",
            "Which operator calculates the average after adding two readings?",
            new[] { "*", "%", "//=", "/" },
