        /* CAVECODE_PYTHON_MODULE_40_RECALLPROMPT_REPAIR */
        "Rebuild the complete facility automation capstone. Use these exact identifiers: can_start, cycle, door_closed, emergency_stop, f, file, level_ok, log_event, message, mode, open, print, pump_running, range, write. Use these exact values: 1, 4, \"AUTO\", \"Emergency stop\", False, \"Monitoring cycle {cycle}\", \"Pump started\", \"Start blocked\", True, \"\\n\", \"facility.log\".",
            /* CAVECODE_PYTHON_MODULE_40_TRANSFERPROMPT_REPAIR */
        /* CAVECODE_PYTHON_MODULE_40_TRANSFERPROMPT_REPAIR */
        "Create a ventilation capstone using AUTO mode, air_quality_ok, smoke_alarm, three monitoring cycles, and event logging. Use these exact identifiers: can_start_fan, cycle, f, fan_running, file, log_event, message, open, print, range, write. Use these exact values: 1, 4, \"Air-quality cycle {cycle}\", False, \"Fan start blocked\", \"Fan started\", \"Smoke shutdown\", True, \"\\n\", \"ventilation.log\".",
            "def can_start_fan(mode, air_quality_ok, smoke_alarm):\n    return mode == \"AUTO\" and air_quality_ok and not smoke_alarm\n\ndef log_event(message):\n    with open(\"ventilation.log\", \"a\") as file:\n        file.write(message + \"\\n\")\n\nmode = \"AUTO\"\nair_quality_ok = True\nsmoke_alarm = False\nfan_running = False\n\nif can_start_fan(mode, air_quality_ok, smoke_alarm):\n    fan_running = True\n    log_event(\"Fan started\")\n    for cycle in range(1, 4):\n        if smoke_alarm:\n            fan_running = False\n            log_event(\"Smoke shutdown\")\n            break\n        print(f\"Air-quality cycle {cycle}\")\nelse:\n    log_event(\"Fan start blocked\")",
            "Course complete: the underground facility is fully automated."
